WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.130
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:17.270
Last time: If · Then · Else

3
00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:26.580
Chapter 5 · Debugging — Finding the Mistake

4
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:38.750
De · bug · ging? Bugs?!

5
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:55.480
Open bag → Books → Tiffin → Walk to school

6
00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:08.360
Oh no! Everything fell out!

7
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:16.100
Is Robo being naughty? Think!

8
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:29.480
Robo followed exactly. A step was wrong.

9
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.840
A mistake in the steps is called a BUG

10
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:48.210
Long ago, a real moth got stuck in a computer!

11
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:56.780
Not an insect. Not a naughty computer.

12
00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:07.990
Debugging = finding the bug and fixing it

13
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:14.160
How to hunt a bug: 3 detective steps

14
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:22.070
1 · Read the steps slowly, one by one

15
00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:39.530
2 · Find where it goes wrong: bag not closed!

16
00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:49.560
3 · Change one thing: add "Close the bag"

17
00:02:49.560 --> 00:03:00.310
Test again → it works! Bug squashed!

18
00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:04.580
Three kinds of bugs

19
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:10.410
Missing step: something was forgotten

20
00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:15.130
Wrong order: right steps, mixed up

21
00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:20.360
Extra step: doesn't belong, take it out

22
00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:37.210
Shoes → Socks → Go outside. What's the bug?

23
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:48.530
Wrong order! Swap: socks first, then shoes

24
00:03:48.530 --> 00:04:04.250
Brush · Paste · Dance on the bed · Brush teeth

25
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:14.840
Extra step! Remove "Dance on the bed"

26
00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:21.170
Why change just one thing at a time?

27
00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:34.060
Changed 3 things at once… which one worked?

28
00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:48.990
One change, then test → you know what worked

29
00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:58.660
True or false? The computer is being naughty.

30
00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:10.260
False! The mistake is in the steps

31
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:21.340
Every programmer finds bugs, every day!

32
00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:33.180
Found a bug? Celebrate! "Bug squashed!"

33
00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.450
Your turn: practice check

34
00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:55.810
Tea steps: what's the bug?

35
00:05:55.810 --> 00:06:10.060
Missing step: boil the water first!

36
00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:17.060
Bug = a mistake in the steps

37
00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.240
Debugging = find it and fix it

38
00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.530
Missing · Extra · Wrong order

39
00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.650
Change one thing, then test

40
00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:41.880
Chapter 5 done · Unit 2 complete!

41
00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:48.680
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
